---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FinalCTA from '@/components/sections/FinalCTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="A/B Testing Service — Split Testing Agency"
  description="We design, run, and analyze A/B tests that produce reliable, revenue-moving results. No false positives. No wasted cycles. Only data-backed wins."
>
  <div class="service-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="breadcrumbs__separator" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a href="/services/">Services</a>
        <span class="breadcrumbs__separator" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span class="breadcrumbs__current" aria-current="page">A/B Testing</span>
      </nav>
      <span class="section-label">Service</span>
      <h1 class="service-hero__title">A/B Testing That Actually Moves Revenue</h1>
      <p class="service-hero__subtitle">
        Most teams run A/B tests wrong — they peek at results early, stop when they see a "winner,"
        and implement changes based on statistical noise. We do it properly.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Start Your Testing Program</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">How Our A/B Testing Works</h2>
      <div class="process-grid">
        {[
          { step: '1', title: 'Research', desc: 'We audit your analytics, run heatmaps, and interview users to form data-backed hypotheses — not gut-feel guesses.' },
          { step: '2', title: 'Design', desc: 'We design test variants based on psychological principles and CRO frameworks, with proper statistical power calculations upfront.' },
          { step: '3', title: 'Run', desc: 'Tests run for the minimum required sample size and time — never stopped early, never peeked at mid-test results.' },
          { step: '4', title: 'Analyze', desc: 'Full segment analysis: device, traffic source, new vs. returning. We extract learning whether the test wins or loses.' },
          { step: '5', title: 'Implement', desc: 'Winners get implemented. Findings feed the next hypothesis. Your test log becomes a competitive moat over time.' },
        ].map(({ step, title, desc }) => (
          <div class="process-step-card">
            <div class="process-step-card__number">{step}</div>
            <h3 class="process-step-card__title">{title}</h3>
            <p class="process-step-card__desc">{desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align:left;">Why Most A/B Tests Fail</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6); color: var(--color-text);">The majority of A/B tests run by marketing teams produce no usable results — not because A/B testing doesn't work, but because tests are designed and stopped incorrectly. The most common mistakes: stopping a test the moment it hits 95% statistical significance (before the required sample size is reached), running tests for less than two full business cycles, and testing cosmetic changes instead of high-impact elements like headlines, value propositions, and form structure.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6); color: var(--color-text);">A properly run A/B test requires three things before it starts: a clear hypothesis grounded in data, a pre-calculated sample size based on your baseline conversion rate and the minimum detectable effect you care about, and a commitment to run the full duration regardless of what interim results show. Without these, you're not testing — you're generating noise.</p>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text);">When tests are done correctly, they compound. Each winning test raises your baseline CVR. Each losing test tells you something valuable about your audience. After 12–18 months of systematic testing, the gap between companies that test well and those that don't becomes decisive. We've run over 800 A/B tests across e-commerce, SaaS, and B2B. We know what moves the needle and what doesn't.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FinalCTA
    title="Ready to Run Tests That Actually Matter?"
    subtitle="Book a free strategy call. We'll review your current testing setup and show you exactly what we'd test first and why."
    ctaText="Book a Free Strategy Call"
  />
</BaseLayout>

